Lucciola: say the common PAM results in words on a failed login

greetd reports a failed login as "<PAM call>: <PAM result>" and the
greeter shows that text as it is, so a wrong password reads
"pam_authenticate: AUTH_ERR". Map the results a person can meet
(wrong password, unknown user, too many attempts, expired account or
password, login not allowed, the auth service not answering) to a
sentence; anything else is shown as greetd sent it, and the log keeps
the raw text in every case.

Applied by lucciola/greeter/noctalia-greeter.spec to the v1.6.0 tag.
Could be proposed upstream (noctalia-dev/noctalia-greeter); the greeter
has no translations yet, so the strings are English like its others.

--- a/src/greeter/greeter_surface.cpp
+++ b/src/greeter/greeter_surface.cpp
@@ -52,6 +52,36 @@
   constexpr float kHeaderUserIconBase = 64.0f;
   constexpr float kHeaderAvatarBorderScale = 2.0f;
 
+  // greetd reports a failed login as "<PAM call>: <PAM result>", for example
+  // "pam_authenticate: AUTH_ERR" for a wrong password. Say the common results
+  // in words; anything else is shown as greetd sent it.
+  std::string authErrorText(const std::string& description) {
+    const auto colon = description.rfind(": ");
+    const std::string result = colon == std::string::npos ? description : description.substr(colon + 2);
+    if (result == "AUTH_ERR") {
+      return "Wrong password, try again";
+    }
+    if (result == "USER_UNKNOWN") {
+      return "Wrong user name or password, try again";
+    }
+    if (result == "MAXTRIES") {
+      return "Too many attempts, wait a moment and try again";
+    }
+    if (result == "ACCT_EXPIRED") {
+      return "This account has expired";
+    }
+    if (result == "NEW_AUTHTOK_REQD" || result == "AUTHTOK_EXPIRED") {
+      return "The password has expired";
+    }
+    if (result == "PERM_DENIED") {
+      return "This account cannot log in here";
+    }
+    if (result == "AUTHINFO_UNAVAIL") {
+      return "The login service did not answer, try again";
+    }
+    return description;
+  }
+
